# vehje-schedule, known gaps

## CompilerSchedule

Skeleton placeholder. Documented inline in `src/lib.rs` as the
target shape for the M0.2 round (#131) that wires every compiler
phase as a hilavitkutin WorkUnit. A dedicated DESIGN.md entry
lands as part of #131 when the real DAG topology, access-set
declaration, and dispatch surface are designed. Currently the type
is a unit-struct harness that returns `ScheduleError::Unimplemented`
on any execution attempt. The harness is shipped now to clear
no-empty-crate so consumer crates can take a workspace path dep.

## ScheduleError

Skeleton placeholder. Skeleton variant set is the single
`Unimplemented` flagging the not-yet-wired state. The full enum
covering DAG cycle detection, access-set conflicts, and missing-pass
diagnostics lands in M0.2 (#131) when the WU-home wiring becomes
concrete. Documented inline in `src/lib.rs` rather than in a
dedicated DESIGN section because the final shape will differ from
the skeleton and a premature design entry risks drift.
